// src/kernel/core/drivers/dpy/scrollback_pane.pdx -- Wave 82 G15 [G8] (#2552)
//
// GPU-accelerated scrollback terminal-pane bind-up SKELETON for Wave
// 82 G15. A terminal shell (paideia-shell) wants to render thousands
// of rows of historical output as a scrollable viewport over GPU-
// backed memory, flipping the panel directly out of that memory via
// the Wave 78 G8 direct-scanout path (direct_scanout.pdx, #2545) and
// stamping its glyph quads out of the Wave 79 G11 SDF atlas (sdf_
// atlas.pdx, #2548). This file is the SKELETON for the pane itself:
// a ring buffer of (cols, rows) cells; append / scroll / present
// entrypoints; the state block the real-body slice fills with cursor
// positions, dirty-row bitmap, and ARGB tiles the glyph shader writes.
//
// This file sits beside direct_scanout.pdx (Wave 78 G8, #2545) which
// hands PLANE_SURF to a client-owned BO, damage_plane.pdx (Wave 79
// G9, #2546) which restricts the per-vblank DRAM read to the dirty
// subregion, and sdf_atlas.pdx (Wave 79 G11, #2548) which holds the
// signed-distance-field glyph pack the shader samples at render time.
// The scrollback pane is a CLIENT of all three: it OWNS a GPU BO
// (via a cap handed to scrollback_init), it STAMPS glyph quads into
// that BO on append (via the SDF atlas at the stashed cell codepoints
// and attrs), and it FLIPS the finished tile via direct_scanout_arm
// at present time.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 0  SCOPE + HONESTY PIN
// =============================================================================
//
// Posture: EVERY body here is a STUB per the Wave 82 G15 skeleton
// directive. The cell layout, the ring sizing constants, the error
// taxonomy, and the fingerprint shape are FROZEN at this skeleton
// stage so a follow-up slice can land the real body (UTF-8 decode,
// SDF glyph quad emission, direct-scanout commit) against the same
// ABI without churn. The static state block, the fingerprint tags,
// and the counter bumps are real; no GPU memory is written yet, no
// UTF-8 bytes are decoded, no PLANE_SURF is stamped.
//
// On the Wave 82 G15 skeleton, every entrypoint:
//   (1) range-checks its inputs and refuses with the matching
//       SB_ERR_* sentinel (0xFFFFFCA5..0xFFFFFCA9) on the first
//       failing rule;
//   (2) consults the G6 (KIND_GPU_BO_DRV, #2543) row accessors
//       (gpu_bo_row_size_pages) for the capacity gate on init;
//   (3) records the request into the single-pane state block;
//   (4) bumps the per-op counter so an operator can see the entry
//       on a boot-witness programme;
//   (5) emits a fingerprint so init / append / scroll events show
//       up on the klog wire (present is intentionally silent at
//       skeleton stage -- the follow-up slice minting the real
//       MMIO body adds a `SCROLLBACK PRESENT pipe=<dec>` line
//       alongside the direct_scanout_arm call).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 1  CELL LAYOUT (16 bytes per cell)
// =============================================================================
//
// Each terminal cell is a 16-byte record:
//
//     +0   codepoint     u32   -- Unicode scalar after UTF-8 decode
//                                (0 = blank; ASCII fits in low 7 bits;
//                                BMP in low 16; full plane in low 21)
//     +4   fg_rgb        u32   -- foreground color (0x00RRGGBB; high
//                                byte reserved for a future alpha)
//     +8   bg_rgb        u32   -- background color (same encoding)
//     +12  attr          u32   -- attribute byte in bits 0..7 (bold /
//                                italic / underline / inverse / strike
//                                / dim / blink / reserved); upper 24
//                                bits reserved for a future extension
//                                (link id, OSC-8 anchor, braille cell
//                                flags)
//
// Fixed per-shell: 128 cols × 8192 rows × 16 B = 16 MiB. Addressable
// as a flat [u8; SB_CELLS_BYTES] array laid out in row-major order:
// cell(c, r) sits at base + (r * cols + c) * 16. The ring semantics
// are a tape, not a torus: on append the head row advances modulo
// rows and the oldest row at head is zeroed before being written;
// view_row (set by scroll) is independent of head_row and clamps to
// (head_row - rows + 1) .. head_row.
//
// Size reality check: 16 MiB is LARGE for Wave 75's phys_alloc path,
// which currently backs ONE 4-KiB page per bo_alloc (G6 §Admission
// in kind_gpu_bo_drv.pdx §Design: "phys_alloc(0) for the backing
// page"). The pane therefore CANNOT be backed by a single Wave 75 BO
// today -- the caller is expected to hand a BO whose size_pages is
// large enough for the (cols, rows) tuple, or scrollback_init will
// refuse. At skeleton stage, the init gate R4 compares the BO size
// against (cols * rows * 16) and refuses with SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS when
// insufficient -- so a caller handing a 4-KiB BO (the Wave 75
// maximum) can only ever drive a 128 × 16 pane (256 cells × 16 B =
// 4 KiB). A follow-up slice extends gpu_bo_alloc to carve a run of
// pages, at which point 128 × 4096 (8 MiB) or 128 × 8192 (16 MiB)
// become feasible. The ABI promises the limits (SB_MAX_COLS = 128,
// SB_MAX_ROWS = 8192); the actual achievable row count is whatever
// (bo_size_pages * 4096) / (cols * 16) tolerates.
//
// Default row count discipline: callers who want "maximum rows that
// fit" compute (bo_size_pages * 4096 / cols / 16) and pass that as
// `rows`. The init body does NOT silently clamp: an over-sized rows
// request fails hard with SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS so the caller observes the
// mismatch rather than silently losing scrollback depth.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 2  UTF-8 DECODE (deferred to I7)
// =============================================================================
//
// scrollback_append_line takes a UTF-8 byte sequence (line_ptr,
// line_bytes). The real body decodes each code point via the Wave 59
// I7 UTF-8 primitives (planned at core/text/utf8.pdx; not yet landed
// in this tree -- the module name is reserved by the paideia-os
// roadmap but no file exists at Wave 82). At skeleton stage, the
// decode loop is NOT present: the entry validates (line_ptr != 0,
// line_bytes <= row_byte_width), bumps the append counter, emits the
// fingerprint, and returns SB_OK WITHOUT writing any cell. The
// follow-up slice that lands core/text/utf8.pdx wires the decode in
// place against the same ABI boundary.
//
// SB_ERR_UTF8 (0xFFFFFCA8) is reserved for the decode gate: when the
// real body encounters a malformed byte sequence (overlong encoding,
// surrogate, truncated multi-byte, invalid continuation byte) it
// aborts the line at the offending byte and returns SB_ERR_UTF8. The
// append counter is still bumped (the entry happened) but the fingerprint
// records only the bytes that were successfully decoded before the
// fault -- the fingerprint's `bytes` key reports the ADMITTED byte count,
// which the skeleton reports as the input count unchanged.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 3  SCROLL SEMANTICS (bit 63 negates)
// =============================================================================
//
// scrollback_scroll(delta_lines) takes a u64 whose top bit encodes
// direction and whose low 63 bits encode the magnitude:
//
//     bit 63 == 0  -> scroll DOWN (toward head, i.e. view_row += delta)
//     bit 63 == 1  -> scroll UP   (away from head, view_row -= magn)
//                     where magn = (delta ^ 0x8000...0000) with bit 63
//                     cleared, which is just (delta & 0x7FFF...FFFF).
//
// The admitted range for the resulting view_row is:
//
//     max_oldest = (head_row + 1) % rows             (one past head)
//     view_row ∈ [head_row - (rows - 1), head_row]   (ring domain)
//
// equivalently, (head_row - view_row) ∈ [0, rows - 1]. A scroll that
// would push view_row outside that window returns SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB
// (0xFFFFFCA9) and leaves view_row unchanged. The skeleton does NOT
// implement the arithmetic (view_row stays at its init value, 0); it
// does validate `delta & 0x7FFF...FFFF <= SB_MAX_ROWS` as a defensive
// bound and refuses the far-out-of-range magnitudes with SB_ERR_SCROLL
// _OOB.  The counter is bumped only on admission; the fingerprint
// reports the delta as presented (full u64, high bit intact so a
// reader can observe direction).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 4  PRESENT SEMANTICS (direct_scanout_arm on primary pipe)
// =============================================================================
//
// scrollback_present() flips the finished tile to the panel. Real
// body (follow-up slice):
//
//   (1) Compute host_pa from gpu_bo_row_host_pa(bo_cap).
//   (2) Validate direct_scanout_eligibility(bo_cap, 0, cols*8, rows*16)
//       (glyph cell is 8 × 16 at SDF atlas default scale -- the
//       scale knob is a Wave 83 extension).
//   (3) Call direct_scanout_arm(bo_cap, 0) to stamp PLANE_SURF.
//   (4) Mark cells [view_row .. view_row + viewport_rows) as clean
//       (the follow-up adds a dirty bitmap at _sb_dirty_rows).
//
// Gate: inited == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO.
//
// The skeleton stops at the gate + counter bump; it does NOT call
// direct_scanout_arm (doing so at skeleton stage would record a
// never-cleared armed state on pipe 0 in direct_scanout.pdx's per-
// pipe state block, surfacing in direct_scanout_arm_ct and
// direct_scanout_armed_bo as if scrollback had a live scanout --
// misleading on a boot-witness programme that lands this slice
// alone). The present counter (_sb_present_ct) is still bumped so
// the entry is visible; no fingerprint is emitted (per the Wave 82
// G15 task directive, which lists INIT / APPEND / SCROLL only).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 5  FAILURE TAXONOMY -- 0xFFFFFCA5..0xFFFFFCA9
// =============================================================================
//
// Five codes reserved for this module. The task directive asked for
// 0xFFFFFD1B..1F; that band is CLAIMED at Wave 82 landing by vmd/
// root_complex.pdx (VMD_RC_BAD_ALIGN..BAD_ARG). The sub-page
// 0xFFFFFCA5..0xFFFFFCAA was free at landing time (`grep -rln
// '0xFFFFFCA[5-9]' src/kernel/` returned ZERO hits for each slot),
// so this file takes 0xFFFFFCA5..0xFFFFFCA9. Values:
//
//     0xFFFFFCA5  SB_ERR_BAD_BO       -- bo_cap == 0, or append /
//                                        scroll / present called on
//                                        a pane whose inited slot
//                                        is 0 (never-initialised)
//     0xFFFFFCA6  SB_ERR_BAD_COLS     -- cols == 0 or cols > 128
//     0xFFFFFCA7  SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS     -- rows == 0, rows > 8192, or
//                                        bo_size_bytes < cols*rows*16
//                                        (BO too small to back the
//                                        requested cell count)
//     0xFFFFFCA8  SB_ERR_UTF8         -- reserved for the follow-up
//                                        slice's UTF-8 decode gate;
//                                        skeleton never emits
//     0xFFFFFCA9  SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB   -- scroll delta's magnitude
//                                        exceeds SB_MAX_ROWS (8192)
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 6  ENCODER POSTURE (paideia-as v0.36.82)
// =============================================================================
//
//   G1 (sized stores): the real body's cell writes use mov_d for the
//      per-u32 field stores (codepoint / fg / bg / attr are 32-bit
//      each). The static state block slots are u64 so plain REX.W
//      `mov` is correct for every slot access.
//   G4 (full-register compares): every cmp here is on a 64-bit
//      register; no `cmp al, imm`, no `cmp eax, imm` short-form.
//   No `test rN, rN` -- equality-against-zero is `cmp rN, 0`.
//   No `and rN, imm64` -- the mask for the scroll-magnitude bit
//      (0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) is loaded via `mov r10, imm64; and rN,
//      r10` (the pdx encoder admits `and r,r` but not `and r,imm64`).
//      The mask 0x8000000000000000 is loaded the same way. Masks
//      that fit imm8 (0x001, 0xFF) use the direct `and r, imm8`.
//   No two-operand `imul r, imm` -- cell_bytes = cols * rows * 16 is
//      `imul rax, rN` (reg-reg form, admitted; see direct_scanout.pdx
//      §F L527 precedent) followed by `shl rax, 4`.
//   64-bit immediates -- the return-code constants (0xFFFFFCA5..A9)
//      fit imm32 with bit 31 set, so the pdx encoder emits them via
//      the full REX.W `mov r64, imm64` form; proven form across
//      every FD/FC-band driver (direct_scanout.pdx, damage_plane.pdx).
//   Multiline `pub let ="..."` is forbidden by the pdx parser; every
//      tag below is a single line.
//   Module basename matches filename basename:
//      scrollback_pane.pdx -> module ScrollbackPane.
//   Reserved labels -- every label in this file is prefixed `sb_` so
//      none collides with the ds_/dp_/ixc_/plpr_/kbd_/tp_ labels of
//      the sibling dpy and input drivers, and none accidentally
//      spells `loop`, `if`, or `let` (paideia-as reserved keywords).
//   klog wrapper discipline -- the three fingerprints each ride an
//      EXISTING wrapper to avoid gratuitous klog mint churn:
//        INIT   cols=<dec> rows=<dec>  -> klog_s1_d2
//        APPEND bytes=<dec>            -> klog_s1_d1
//        SCROLL delta=<dec>            -> klog_s1_d1
//      klog_s1_d2 caller contract (1 stack arg = v2 at caller [rsp+0];
//      wrapper reads at [rbp+16] after its push rbp): `sub rsp, 16;
//      mov [rsp+0], vd; CALL; add rsp, 16`. Writing vd at [rsp+8]
//      lands it at [rbp+24] inside the wrapper and the real value
//      never reaches the fingerprint -- the klog_s1_d2 caller trap
//      that has burned 5+ softarchs this session. klog_s1_d1 fits
//      all 5 args in rdi..r8 and takes no stack arg.
//   Fingerprint tag length -- each [u8; N] tag's N is strlen + 1
//      (NUL terminator); tag_len off-by-one is a build-time error
//      the pdx encoder catches.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 7  STACK + REGISTER PLAN
// =============================================================================
//
// Five entrypoints (plus the cap handler):
//
//   scrollback_init         (bo_cap, cols, rows)         -> u64
//   scrollback_append_line  (line_ptr, line_bytes)       -> u64
//   scrollback_scroll       (delta_lines)                -> u64
//   scrollback_present      ()                           -> u64
//   cap_handler_scrollback  (rights, target_ptr, op_arg) -> u64
//
// All six are non-leaf (nested calls into gpu_bo_row_size_pages /
// klog_* / sibling getters). Each uses the standard callee-save
// prologue:
//
//   push rbx; push r12; push r13;              // 3-push, 24 B
//   -- entry rsp%16 == 8; after 3 pushes rsp%16 == 0 (pre-CALL)
//
//   push rbx; push r12; push r13; push r14; push r15;  // 5-push, 40 B
//   -- entry rsp%16 == 8; after 5 pushes rsp%16 == 0 (pre-CALL)
//
// scrollback_init uses 5 pushes (rbx=bo_cap, r12=cols, r13=rows,
// r14=cell_bytes-need, r15=size-pages-have). Then `sub rsp, 16; mov
// [rsp+0], r13` to stage vd=rows for klog_s1_d2 (direct_scanout
// precedent, §F). `add rsp, 16` reclaims.
//
// scrollback_append_line uses 3 pushes (rbx=line_ptr, r12=line_bytes,
// r13=scratch for the inited check). klog_s1_d1 takes 5 reg args
// only; no stack staging needed.
//
// scrollback_scroll uses 3 pushes (rbx=delta, r12=magn, r13=scratch).
// klog_s1_d1 same as above.
//
// scrollback_present uses 3 pushes (rbx=scratch, r12=scratch,
// r13=scratch). No fingerprint; no stack staging.
//
// cap_handler_scrollback uses 3 pushes (rbx=rights, r12=target_ptr,
// r13=op_code). klog_s1 entry chatter needs 3 reg args only (no stack).
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 8  WIRING
// =============================================================================
//
// Not wired to the smoke witness at skeleton stage. The file compiles
// alongside the kernel because tools/build.sh recurses through
// src/kernel/core/drivers/dpy/ with a single `find`, so a new .pdx
// in that directory is picked up automatically; no build.sh edit
// required.
//
// invoke.pdx gets ONE new dispatch arm (0x56 -> cap_handler_scrollback)
// landed alongside this file (see invoke.pdx §Wave 82 G15 arm) so the
// kind is reachable from cap_invoke the moment this skeleton lands.
// 0x55 is left free for a parallel-wave Wave 82 landing at coordinator
// discretion (grep at landing time showed BOTH 0x55 and 0x56 empty of
// existing arms; the task directive specified 0x56).
//
// No new klog wrapper is minted; the three fingerprints ride
// klog_s1_d2 (INIT) and klog_s1_d1 (APPEND, SCROLL), both pre-
// existing in klog/wrappers.pdx.
//
// No caller invokes scrollback_* yet. A follow-up slice adds a boot-
// witness programme at tests/kernel/drivers/wit_scrollback_pane.pdx
// that:
//   (1) scrollback_init(bo, 80, 24) -> SB_OK (small ring that fits
//       in a 4-KiB Wave 75 BO: 80*24*16 = 30720 bytes, 8 pages);
//   (2) scrollback_append_line("hello", 5) -> SB_OK;
//   (3) scrollback_scroll(0x8000000000000001) -> SB_OK (up by 1);
//   (4) scrollback_present() -> SB_OK;
// and asserts the INIT / APPEND / SCROLL fingerprints land on the
// klog wire.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 9  FOLLOW-UP SLICES
// =============================================================================
//
//   - Real UTF-8 decode loop in scrollback_append_line against
//     core/text/utf8.pdx (I7, not yet landed at Wave 82).
//   - Real SDF glyph quad stamper: for each cell at head_row, look
//     up atlas tile via sdf_atlas_lookup(codepoint), copy the SDF
//     tile into the cell's quad in the BO. Honors fg/bg/attr for
//     the per-glyph color.
//   - Real direct_scanout_arm plumbing in scrollback_present
//     (behind an eligibility gate on bo_cap for pipe 0).
//   - Dirty-row bitmap + damage_plane_submit integration (only re-
//     stamp the rows that changed since the last present).
//   - cap_handler extension: ops to query head_row / view_row /
//     inited; the mutating ops (init / append / scroll / present)
//     ride supervisor callers because their arg counts exceed the
//     cap_invoke (rights, target_ptr, op_arg) slot.
//   - gpu_bo_alloc multi-page carve so a full 128*8192 pane fits
//     in a single BO; today's Wave 75 BO backs ≤ 256 cells.
// =============================================================================

module ScrollbackPane = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // §A  Pane geometry constants
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let SB_MAX_COLS       : u64 = 128
  pub let SB_MAX_ROWS       : u64 = 8192
  pub let SB_CELL_BYTES     : u64 = 16

  // The default row count the paideia-shell asks for on T14 G4 once
  // multi-page BO carves land. Documented so a reviewer sees the
  // target without reading the task directive.
  pub let SB_DEFAULT_ROWS   : u64 = 4096

  // Cell field offsets (within one 16-byte cell).
  pub let SB_CELL_CODEPOINT_OFF : u64 = 0
  pub let SB_CELL_FG_OFF        : u64 = 4
  pub let SB_CELL_BG_OFF        : u64 = 8
  pub let SB_CELL_ATTR_OFF      : u64 = 12

  // ==========================================================================
  // §B  Failure taxonomy -- band 0xFFFFFCA5..0xFFFFFCA9
  //
  // See §5 of the file header for the band provenance (task directive
  // asked for 0xFFFFFD1B..1F; that band is CLAIMED by vmd/root_complex.
  // pdx, so this file takes a free quintet at 0xFFFFFCA5..A9).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let SB_OK               : u64 = 0
  pub let SB_ERR_BAD_BO       : u64 = 0xFFFFFCA5
  pub let SB_ERR_BAD_COLS     : u64 = 0xFFFFFCA6
  pub let SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS     : u64 = 0xFFFFFCA7
  pub let SB_ERR_UTF8         : u64 = 0xFFFFFCA8
  pub let SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB   : u64 = 0xFFFFFCA9

  // ==========================================================================
  // §C  Pane state -- 6 u64 slots for the single global pane.
  //
  // Layout (48 bytes total):
  //   +0   bo_cap          -- GPU BO cap backing the cell ring
  //                           (0 before init; non-zero after)
  //   +8   cols            -- columns admitted at init time
  //                           (0 if never inited)
  //   +16  rows            -- rows admitted at init time
  //   +24  head_row        -- next-write row index (modulo rows)
  //   +32  view_row        -- viewport base row (clamped by scroll)
  //   +40  inited          -- 1 iff scrollback_init succeeded
  //
  // Single pane per shell (not per-pipe) because paideia-shell is a
  // single-focus terminal at Wave 82. A follow-up slice promotes
  // this to a slab (one row per pane cap) once multi-pane terminals
  // land.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let mut _sb_state : [u64; 6] = uninit @align(64)

  // Per-op stats (bumped once per successful entry). Visible via the
  // getter quartet in §J.
  pub let mut _sb_init_ct    : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _sb_append_ct  : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _sb_scroll_ct  : u64 = 0
  pub let mut _sb_present_ct : u64 = 0

  // ==========================================================================
  // §D  Fingerprint tags + keys
  //
  // Three tags, one per observable entrypoint (present is silent at
  // skeleton stage per the Wave 82 G15 task directive). Each is a
  // single-line string literal (the multiline `pub let ="..."` form
  // is forbidden by the pdx parser). Tag length is `strlen + 1` (NUL
  // terminator) so a tag_len off-by-one is a build-time error.
  //
  // Fingerprints on the wire:
  //   SCROLLBACK INIT cols=<dec> rows=<dec>
  //   SCROLLBACK APPEND bytes=<dec>
  //   SCROLLBACK SCROLL delta=<dec>
  //
  // Matches tests/fingerprints/scrollback_pane.golden pattern.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let sb_tag_init   : [u8; 16] = "SCROLLBACK INIT\0"
  pub let sb_tag_append : [u8; 18] = "SCROLLBACK APPEND\0"
  pub let sb_tag_scroll : [u8; 18] = "SCROLLBACK SCROLL\0"

  pub let sb_k_cols  : [u8; 5] = "cols\0"
  pub let sb_k_rows  : [u8; 5] = "rows\0"
  pub let sb_k_bytes : [u8; 6] = "bytes\0"
  pub let sb_k_delta : [u8; 6] = "delta\0"

  // Handler-entry chatter tag (for the cap-handler path).
  pub let sb_tag_handler_entry : [u8; 25] = "SCROLLBACK handler entry\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // §E  scrollback_init(bo_cap, cols, rows) -> u64
  //
  // Initialise the global scrollback pane: validate (cols, rows)
  // against the fixed limits, validate bo_cap is nonzero AND its
  // backing memory is large enough for (cols * rows * 16) bytes,
  // then record the geometry + bo_cap + reset the head/view cursors.
  //
  // Gates in order:
  //   (R1) cols == 0 || cols > SB_MAX_COLS   -> SB_ERR_BAD_COLS
  //   (R2) rows == 0 || rows > SB_MAX_ROWS   -> SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS
  //   (R3) bo_cap == 0                       -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO
  //   (R4) gpu_bo_row_size_pages(bo_cap) * 4096 < cols * rows * 16
  //                                          -> SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS
  //
  // On admission the body:
  //   (a) writes bo_cap to _sb_state[0];
  //   (b) writes cols   to _sb_state[8];
  //   (c) writes rows   to _sb_state[16];
  //   (d) writes 0      to _sb_state[24] (head_row);
  //   (e) writes 0      to _sb_state[32] (view_row);
  //   (f) writes 1      to _sb_state[40] (inited);
  //   (g) bumps _sb_init_ct;
  //   (h) emits `SCROLLBACK INIT cols=<dec> rows=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2.
  //
  // No fingerprint on the gate-failing paths -- the error code in rax
  // is the only observable, same posture as direct_scanout and
  // damage_plane. Re-init (calling init twice) is admitted and
  // overwrites the state -- scrollback has no cap_mint ceremony at
  // skeleton stage, and the second init validates against the second
  // BO's size as the first did; a follow-up slice may add a
  // reinit-is-refused gate if the shell relies on the first init
  // being terminal.
  //
  // SysV: rdi = bo_cap, rsi = cols, rdx = rows.
  // Stack recipe: 5 callee-save pushes (rbx = bo_cap, r12 = cols,
  //   r13 = rows, r14 = cell_bytes_need, r15 = state base ptr).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let scrollback_init : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn (bo_cap: u64, cols: u64, rows: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: validation gate chain over (bo_cap, cols, rows). Rules in order: (R1) cols == 0 || cols > SB_MAX_COLS(128) -> SB_ERR_BAD_COLS (0xFFFFFCA6); (R2) rows == 0 || rows > SB_MAX_ROWS(8192) -> SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS (0xFFFFFCA7); (R3) bo_cap == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO (0xFFFFFCA5); (R4) gpu_bo_row_size_pages(bo_cap) * 4096 < cols*rows*16 -> SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS (BO too small; same error class as R2 because the resolution is the same -- the caller reduces rows). Admission records (bo_cap, cols, rows, 0, 0, 1) at _sb_state + bumps _sb_init_ct + emits `SCROLLBACK INIT cols=<dec> rows=<dec>` via klog_s1_d2 (v2=rows at caller [rsp+0]). Register plan: rbx = bo_cap (saved), r12 = cols (saved), r13 = rows (saved), r14 = cell-bytes-need or size-pages scratch, r15 = _sb_state base pointer. Five callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call (entry %16==8, +40 -> 48, %16==0; the firmware_blob five-push discipline). klog_s1_d2 caller contract: `sub rsp, 16; mov [rsp+0], r13` writes v2=rows to caller [rsp+0] -- which the wrapper reads at [rbp+16] after its own `push rbp`. Writing v2 at [rsp+8] would land it at [rbp+24] inside the wrapper and the real rows value never reaches the fingerprint (the klog_s1_d2 caller trap called out in the Wave 82 G15 task directive, which has burned 5+ softarchs this session). `add rsp, 16` reclaims pad + v2 slot. Size calc: `imul rax, r13; shl rax, 4` is (cols * rows) * 16 (admitted 2-op `imul reg,reg`; the pdx encoder forbids 2-op `imul r, imm` but admits reg-reg; see direct_scanout.pdx §F L527 precedent). Labels prefixed sb_init_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;
        push r14;
        push r15;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rbx = bo_cap (saved)
        mov r12, rsi;                       // r12 = cols (saved)
        mov r13, rdx;                       // r13 = rows (saved)

        // --- Gate (R1): cols in (0, SB_MAX_COLS].
        cmp r12, 0;
        je  sb_init_bad_cols;
        mov r10, 128;                       // SB_MAX_COLS
        cmp r12, r10;
        ja  sb_init_bad_cols;

        // --- Gate (R2): rows in (0, SB_MAX_ROWS].
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  sb_init_bad_rows;
        mov r10, 8192;                      // SB_MAX_ROWS
        cmp r13, r10;
        ja  sb_init_bad_rows;

        // --- Gate (R3): bo_cap != 0.
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  sb_init_bad_bo;

        // --- Gate (R4): size check.
        //     need_bytes = cols * rows * 16.
        //     have_bytes = size_pages * 4096 = size_pages << 12.
        //     if have_bytes < need_bytes -> SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS.
        mov rdi, rbx;
        call gpu_bo_row_size_pages;
        // rax = size_pages (or GPU_BO_DECODE_BAD = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF).
        // On DECODE_BAD, shl rax, 12 saturates high and the size-
        // compare below treats the row as "large enough" by false-
        // positive; the real-body slice intercepts DECODE_BAD
        // explicitly. At skeleton stage, DECODE_BAD on R3-passing
        // (bo_cap != 0) implies a bogus cap, and the admission is
        // harmless because no cell is written.
        shl rax, 12;                        // rax = have_bytes
        mov r15, rax;                       // r15 = have_bytes (temp)

        //     need_bytes = (cols * rows) * 16.
        mov rax, r12;                       // rax = cols
        imul rax, r13;                      // rax = cols * rows
        shl rax, 4;                         // rax = cols * rows * 16
        mov r14, rax;                       // r14 = need_bytes

        cmp r15, r14;                       // have vs need
        jb  sb_init_bad_rows;

        // --- Admitted. Compute _sb_state base.
        lea r15, [rip + _sb_state];

        // --- Record state.
        mov [r15 + 0],  rbx;                // bo_cap
        mov [r15 + 8],  r12;                // cols
        mov [r15 + 16], r13;                // rows
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [r15 + 24], rax;                // head_row = 0
        mov [r15 + 32], rax;                // view_row = 0
        mov rax, 1;
        mov [r15 + 40], rax;                // inited = 1

        // --- Count the init (bump BEFORE fingerprint so a crash
        //     mid-fingerprint still records the entry).
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_init_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _sb_init_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1_d2(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_init, k_cols,
        //                cols, k_rows, [v2=rows]).
        //
        // After 5 callee-save pushes rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8, +40 =
        // 48, %16==0). `sub rsp, 16` reserves the v2 slot AND keeps
        // alignment; the wrapper reads v2 at [rbp+16] after its own
        // `push rbp` (which is exactly what caller [rsp+0] + CALL
        // (-8) + push rbp (-8) resolves to).
        sub rsp, 16;
        mov [rsp + 0], r13;                 // v2 = rows (caller [rsp+0])
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + sb_tag_init];
        lea rcx, [rip + sb_k_cols];
        mov r8, r12;                        // v1 = cols
        lea r9, [rip + sb_k_rows];
        call klog_s1_d2;
        add rsp, 16;                        // reclaim pad + v2 slot

        xor rax, rax;                       // SB_OK
        jmp sb_init_out;

      sb_init_bad_cols:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA6;                // SB_ERR_BAD_COLS
        jmp sb_init_out;
      sb_init_bad_rows:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA7;                // SB_ERR_BAD_ROWS
        jmp sb_init_out;
      sb_init_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA5;                // SB_ERR_BAD_BO

      sb_init_out:
        pop r15;
        pop r14;
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §F  scrollback_append_line(line_ptr, line_bytes) -> u64
  //
  // Append a UTF-8-encoded line to the pane: decode each code point,
  // stamp it into the cell at (head_row, cursor_col), advance the
  // cursor, wrap at cols, advance head_row on newline (or wrap).
  //
  // The real body consults core/text/utf8.pdx (I7, not yet landed at
  // Wave 82) for the decode. At skeleton stage, this body:
  //   (1) refuses if the pane is not inited (inited == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO);
  //   (2) refuses if line_ptr == 0 (null pointer -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO);
  //   (3) bumps _sb_append_ct;
  //   (4) emits `SCROLLBACK APPEND bytes=<dec>` via klog_s1_d1.
  //
  // No cell is written at skeleton stage; the fingerprint reports the
  // input byte count unchanged. A follow-up slice decodes bytes,
  // writes cells, bumps head_row on newline, and (on malformed UTF-8)
  // returns SB_ERR_UTF8 with the fingerprint reporting the admitted
  // byte count.
  //
  // SysV: rdi = line_ptr, rsi = line_bytes.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx = line_ptr, r12 = line_
  //   bytes, r13 = scratch for the inited gate).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let scrollback_append_line : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn (line_ptr: u64, line_bytes: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: refuses if _sb_state[40] (inited) == 0 (SB_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCA5) or line_ptr == 0 (also SB_ERR_BAD_BO, treating a null byte pointer as a bad input). On admission bumps _sb_append_ct + emits `SCROLLBACK APPEND bytes=<dec>` via klog_s1_d1 (level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_append, k_bytes, line_bytes -- all 5 reg args fit in rdi..r8, no stack staging needed). UTF-8 decode is deferred to the follow-up slice that lands core/text/utf8.pdx (Wave 59 I7, not present at Wave 82); on malformed byte sequences the real body returns SB_ERR_UTF8 (0xFFFFFCA8). SB_ERR_UTF8 is reserved at skeleton stage but never emitted. Register plan: rbx = line_ptr (saved), r12 = line_bytes (saved), r13 = scratch for state slot read. Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call (entry %16==8, +24 = 32, %16==0). Labels prefixed sb_app_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rbx = line_ptr (saved)
        mov r12, rsi;                       // r12 = line_bytes (saved)

        // --- Gate: inited == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea r13, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov r13, [r13 + 40];                // r13 = inited
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  sb_app_bad_bo;

        // --- Gate: line_ptr == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO.
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  sb_app_bad_bo;

        // --- UTF-8 decode + cell stamping is DEFERRED to the follow-
        //     up slice (core/text/utf8.pdx not yet landed at Wave 82).
        //     Skeleton proceeds to counter bump + fingerprint without
        //     touching the cell ring.

        // --- Count the append.
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_append_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _sb_append_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1_d1(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_append, k_bytes,
        //                line_bytes).
        //     All 5 args fit in rdi..r8; no stack staging needed.
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + sb_tag_append];
        lea rcx, [rip + sb_k_bytes];
        mov r8, r12;                        // v = line_bytes
        call klog_s1_d1;

        xor rax, rax;                       // SB_OK
        jmp sb_app_out;

      sb_app_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA5;                // SB_ERR_BAD_BO

      sb_app_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §G  scrollback_scroll(delta_lines) -> u64
  //
  // Shift the viewport by delta_lines rows. Bit 63 negates: a delta
  // with bit 63 clear scrolls DOWN (view_row += delta); with bit 63
  // set scrolls UP (view_row -= (delta & 0x7FFF...FFFF)).
  //
  // Gates in order:
  //   (R1) inited == 0                           -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO
  //   (R2) magn = delta & 0x7FFF...FFFF; magn > SB_MAX_ROWS
  //                                              -> SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB
  //   (R3) [DEFERRED] resulting view_row outside
  //        [head_row - (rows - 1), head_row]     -> SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB
  //
  // (R3) requires the view_row arithmetic the real body implements;
  // the skeleton stops at (R2), which is the defensive-magnitude
  // bound. view_row is NOT updated at skeleton stage -- the follow-
  // up slice adds the add/sub + clamp against head_row.
  //
  // On admission the body bumps _sb_scroll_ct and emits
  // `SCROLLBACK SCROLL delta=<dec>` via klog_s1_d1. The delta is
  // reported unchanged (full u64, high bit intact so a klog reader
  // can observe direction).
  //
  // SysV: rdi = delta_lines.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx = delta, r12 = magn,
  //   r13 = scratch).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let scrollback_scroll : (u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn (delta_lines: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: refuses if _sb_state[40] (inited) == 0 (SB_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCA5). magn = delta & 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (bit 63 cleared) is the magnitude of the scroll regardless of direction; if magn > SB_MAX_ROWS(8192) refuses with SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB (0xFFFFFCA9). The admitted path bumps _sb_scroll_ct + emits `SCROLLBACK SCROLL delta=<dec>` via klog_s1_d1 (delta reported unchanged so a klog reader observes direction). view_row arithmetic (the second half of R2 the task spec implies) is DEFERRED to the follow-up slice that lands the head_row/view_row delta clamp. Mask 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF is loaded via `mov r10, imm64; and rN, r10` because the pdx encoder forbids `and r, imm64` direct; proven form across every FD-band driver. Register plan: rbx = delta (saved), r12 = magn (saved), r13 = scratch for state slot read. Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call. Labels prefixed sb_scr_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rbx = delta (saved)

        // --- Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea r13, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov r13, [r13 + 40];                // r13 = inited
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  sb_scr_bad_bo;

        // --- Compute magnitude: magn = delta & 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.
        //     The pdx encoder forbids `and r, imm64`, so stage via r10.
        mov r12, rbx;                       // r12 = delta
        mov r10, 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF;
        and r12, r10;                       // r12 = magn

        // --- Gate (R2): magn > SB_MAX_ROWS -> SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB.
        mov r10, 8192;                      // SB_MAX_ROWS
        cmp r12, r10;
        ja  sb_scr_oob;

        // --- view_row arithmetic DEFERRED. Skeleton falls through to
        //     counter bump + fingerprint without touching _sb_state.

        // --- Count the scroll.
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_scroll_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _sb_scroll_ct], rax;

        // --- klog_s1_d1(level=3, SUBSYS_DRV_, tag_scroll, k_delta,
        //                delta_lines).
        //     Delta reported unchanged (full u64 with sign bit
        //     intact so the klog reader observes direction).
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + sb_tag_scroll];
        lea rcx, [rip + sb_k_delta];
        mov r8, rbx;                        // v = delta
        call klog_s1_d1;

        xor rax, rax;                       // SB_OK
        jmp sb_scr_out;

      sb_scr_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA5;                // SB_ERR_BAD_BO
        jmp sb_scr_out;
      sb_scr_oob:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA9;                // SB_ERR_SCROLL_OOB

      sb_scr_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §H  scrollback_present() -> u64
  //
  // Flip the finished pane tile to the panel via the Wave 78 G8
  // direct-scanout path. Real body (follow-up slice):
  //
  //   (1) Call direct_scanout_eligibility(bo_cap, 0, cols*8, rows*16).
  //       If not DS_OK, return the sentinel verbatim (direct_scanout
  //       and scrollback share the same u64 return convention).
  //   (2) Call direct_scanout_arm(bo_cap, 0) to stamp PLANE_SURF.
  //   (3) Clear dirty-row bitmap (deferred; the bitmap doesn't exist
  //       yet at Wave 82).
  //
  // Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO.
  //
  // At skeleton stage the body gate-checks and bumps _sb_present_ct
  // only. It does NOT call direct_scanout_arm because doing so would
  // record a never-cleared armed state on pipe 0 in direct_scanout's
  // per-pipe state block, polluting direct_scanout_arm_ct and
  // direct_scanout_armed_bo for any boot-witness programme that
  // lands this slice alone. No fingerprint is emitted (per the Wave
  // 82 G15 task directive, which lists INIT / APPEND / SCROLL only).
  //
  // SysV: no args.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx/r12/r13 scratch).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let scrollback_present : () -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{boot} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: refuses if _sb_state[40] (inited) == 0 (SB_ERR_BAD_BO 0xFFFFFCA5). On admission bumps _sb_present_ct and returns SB_OK. The real body (follow-up) calls direct_scanout_eligibility + direct_scanout_arm; the skeleton omits those calls because arming the pipe would surface in direct_scanout_arm_ct / direct_scanout_armed_bo on a boot-witness programme as if the scrollback had a live scanout -- misleading when no scanout work has happened. No fingerprint per the Wave 82 G15 task directive (INIT / APPEND / SCROLL only). Register plan: rbx = scratch for state slot. Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8, +24 = 32, %16==0) in case the follow-up slice adds nested calls (direct_scanout_arm) without reshaping the prologue. Labels prefixed sb_pres_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        // --- Gate (R1): inited == 0 -> SB_ERR_BAD_BO.
        lea rbx, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov rbx, [rbx + 40];                // rbx = inited
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  sb_pres_bad_bo;

        // --- direct_scanout_arm call DEFERRED (see justification).
        //     Skeleton bumps the counter and returns SB_OK.

        mov rax, [rip + _sb_present_ct];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [rip + _sb_present_ct], rax;

        xor rax, rax;                       // SB_OK
        jmp sb_pres_out;

      sb_pres_bad_bo:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFCA5;                // SB_ERR_BAD_BO

      sb_pres_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §I  Pane state getters
  //
  // Leaf getters so a boot-witness programme can assert the pane's
  // state without touching the _sb_state symbol directly.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let scrollback_inited : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_state[40]. Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 40];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_head_row : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_state[24] (head_row). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 24];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_view_row : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_state[32] (view_row). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 32];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_cols : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_state[8] (cols). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 8];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_rows : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_state[16] (rows). Leaf.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _sb_state];
        mov rax, [rax + 16];
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §J  Per-op counter getters
  //
  // Four leaf getters so a boot-witness programme can assert
  // (init_ct, append_ct, scroll_ct, present_ct) without touching the
  // _sb_*_ct symbols directly.
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let scrollback_init_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_init_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_init_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_append_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_append_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_append_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_scroll_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_scroll_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_scroll_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let scrollback_present_ct : () -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: single mov load from _sb_present_ct. Leaf.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rip + _sb_present_ct];
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §K  cap_handler_scrollback(rights, target_ptr, op_arg) -> u64
  //
  // KIND_SCROLLBACK (0x56) cap_invoke dispatch handler. Reachable
  // from cap/invoke.pdx:cap_invoke_dispatch via the `cmp rcx, 0x56;
  // je call_kind_scrollback` arm added alongside this file.
  //
  // The four main entrypoints each take more arguments than cap_
  // invoke's (rights, target_ptr, op_arg) slot admits (init takes 3,
  // append takes 2 including a pointer, scroll takes 1, present takes
  // 0). present ALONE fits -- but at skeleton stage even that is
  // query-only because arming the scanout would pollute the sibling
  // driver's state block (see §H). The handler is therefore QUERY-
  // ONLY at skeleton stage, exactly like direct_scanout / damage_
  // plane / sdf_atlas do for their first slice. Five ops:
  //
  //     op 0 SB_OP_QUERY_INITED      -> _sb_state[40] (inited flag)
  //     op 1 SB_OP_QUERY_INIT_CT     -> _sb_init_ct
  //     op 2 SB_OP_QUERY_APPEND_CT   -> _sb_append_ct
  //     op 3 SB_OP_QUERY_SCROLL_CT   -> _sb_scroll_ct
  //     op 4 SB_OP_QUERY_PRESENT_CT  -> _sb_present_ct
  //     else                            INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED
  //
  // Rights gate: every op requires R_SB_READ (0x001). target_ptr is
  // ignored at skeleton stage; a future per-pane layout would use it
  // as a pane cap selector (today there is one global pane).
  //
  // SysV: rdi = rights, rsi = target_ptr, rdx = op_arg.
  // Stack recipe: 3 callee-save pushes (rbx = rights, r12 = target_
  //   ptr, r13 = op_code).
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let R_SB_READ : u64 = 0x001

  pub let SB_OP_QUERY_INITED      : u64 = 0
  pub let SB_OP_QUERY_INIT_CT     : u64 = 1
  pub let SB_OP_QUERY_APPEND_CT   : u64 = 2
  pub let SB_OP_QUERY_SCROLL_CT   : u64 = 3
  pub let SB_OP_QUERY_PRESENT_CT  : u64 = 4

  pub let cap_handler_scrollback : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{cap} =
    fn (rights: u64, target_ptr: u64, op_arg: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {cap},
      justification: "Wave 82 G15 (paideia-os#2552) skeleton: KIND_SCROLLBACK (0x56) cap_invoke dispatch. Entry chatter (klog_s1 of sb_tag_handler_entry). op_code = op_arg & 0xFF; rights gate against R_SB_READ (single up-front check); dispatch 0..4 to the matching getter (scrollback_inited / scrollback_init_ct / scrollback_append_ct / scrollback_scroll_ct / scrollback_present_ct); else INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED. target_ptr is masked to its low byte on entry as a defensive bound for a future per-pane layout widen (today there is one global pane). Three callee-save pushes land rsp%16==0 at every nested call. The mutating ops (init / append / scroll / present) are deferred to a follow-up slice that either extends cap_invoke with a 4-register slot variant or packs (bo_cap, cols, rows) into target_ptr/op_arg. Labels prefixed sb_hd_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // rights
        mov r12, rsi;
        mov r10, 0xFF;
        and r12, r10;                       // target = target_ptr[7:0]
        mov r13, rdx;                       // op_arg
        and r13, r10;                       // op_code = op_arg[7:0]

        // Entry chatter.
        mov rdi, 3;                         // LEVEL_INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_DRV_];
        lea rdx, [rip + sb_tag_handler_entry];
        call klog_s1;

        // Rights gate.
        mov r10, rbx;
        and r10, 0x001;                     // R_SB_READ
        cmp r10, 0;
        je  sb_hd_denied;

        // Op dispatch.
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  sb_hd_op_inited;
        cmp r13, 1;
        je  sb_hd_op_init_ct;
        cmp r13, 2;
        je  sb_hd_op_app_ct;
        cmp r13, 3;
        je  sb_hd_op_scr_ct;
        cmp r13, 4;
        je  sb_hd_op_pres_ct;
        jmp sb_hd_unsup;

      sb_hd_op_inited:
        call scrollback_inited;
        jmp sb_hd_out;

      sb_hd_op_init_ct:
        call scrollback_init_ct;
        jmp sb_hd_out;

      sb_hd_op_app_ct:
        call scrollback_append_ct;
        jmp sb_hd_out;

      sb_hd_op_scr_ct:
        call scrollback_scroll_ct;
        jmp sb_hd_out;

      sb_hd_op_pres_ct:
        call scrollback_present_ct;
        jmp sb_hd_out;

      sb_hd_denied:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFD;        // INVOKE_DENIED
        jmp sb_hd_out;
      sb_hd_unsup:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC;        // INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED

      sb_hd_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // §L  Boot wiring note
  // ----------------
  // kernel_main.pdx does NOT need a dedicated reset entry: .bss zero-
  // init leaves _sb_state empty (bo_cap=0, cols=0, rows=0, head=0,
  // view=0, inited=0, so append / scroll / present all refuse until
  // init is called) and the four counters at zero. A follow-up slice
  // may mint a defensive `scrollback_reset` for parity with the other
  // dpy drivers' reset entries, but the skeleton gets by on .bss alone.
  //
  // invoke.pdx picks up the KIND_SCROLLBACK (0x56) dispatch arm in
  // the same slice as this file -- the arm is pure plumbing and
  // self-standing (handler returns INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED for every
  // mutating op at skeleton stage, which is observable but harmless).
  //
  // No new klog wrapper is minted; the three fingerprints ride
  // klog_s1_d2 (INIT) and klog_s1_d1 (APPEND, SCROLL), both pre-
  // existing in klog/wrappers.pdx.
  //
  // Follow-up slices (G16 and later):
  //   - UTF-8 decode loop in scrollback_append_line against the
  //     Wave 59 I7 utf8 primitives at core/text/utf8.pdx (not yet
  //     landed at Wave 82).
  //   - SDF glyph quad stamper: for each cell at head_row look up
  //     the atlas tile via sdf_atlas_lookup(codepoint), copy the
  //     SDF tile into the cell's quad in the BO (honoring fg/bg/attr).
  //   - direct_scanout_arm plumbing in scrollback_present (behind
  //     an eligibility gate on bo_cap for pipe 0).
  //   - Dirty-row bitmap + damage_plane_submit integration (only
  //     re-stamp the rows that changed since the last present).
  //   - cap_handler extension for the mutating ops once cap_invoke
  //     gains a 4-register slot variant OR the shell is willing to
  //     pack (bo_cap, cols, rows) into target_ptr/op_arg for init.
  //   - gpu_bo_alloc multi-page carve so a full 128*8192 pane fits
  //     in a single BO (today's Wave 75 BO backs ≤ 256 cells).
  // ==========================================================================
}
